{"name":"Holland Red","hex":"#cb4543","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of linen cloth, originally from Holland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holland"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holland","blocks":[{"text":"Holland is a geographical region and former province on the western coast of the Netherlands. From the 10th to the 16th century, Holland proper was a unified political region within the Holy Roman Empire as a county ruled by the counts of Holland. By the 17th century, the province of Holland had risen to become a maritime and economic power, dominating the other provinces of the newly independent Dutch Republic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Holland_position.svg/330px-Holland_position.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holland","wikidata":"Q102911"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Netherlands by population density by province (2006)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANetherlands_Density.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/1280px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of Holland (1682)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif/500px-Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif/500px-Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Holland","link"